The attached image shows flow cytometry plots and bar graphs illustrating how Nano-11 facilitates antigen transport to draining lymph nodes. Panel A displays the detection and phenotyping of OVA-positive cells in these lymph nodes on days 1 and 2, showing that Nano-11-adjuvanted OVA maintains a higher percentage of OVA+ cells compared to soluble OVA. Panel B indicates that Nano-11 significantly increases the mean fluorescence intensity (MFI) of OVA in antigen-containing cells, suggesting enhanced antigen uptake per cell. Panel C reveals that Nano-11 increases the percentage of migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) among OVA-positive cells, highlighting its role in targeting antigen to these immunopotentiating cells more effectively than soluble OVA or aluminum hydroxide adjuvant.